Bits.Description:
Line state of D+ and D-. Shows the filtered LineState or the RX CMD line state of the PHY.

Usage: Read for debug; the value follows the bus and changes without notice.

Values:
0x0 SE0 (reset value);
0x1 J state;
0x2 K state;
0x3 SE1 or reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Negotiated bus speed. Shows the speed set by the chirp handshake or by the attached device.

Usage: Read after the enum interrupt; undefined while detached.

Values:
0x0 high-speed;
0x1 full-speed (reset value);
0x2 low-speed;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Role parameter. Reports PARA_USB2_ROLE of this build.

Usage: Read by the driver at probe time.

Values:
0x0 device only;
0x1 host only;
0x2 dual-role (reset value);
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Test mode selector. Starts a USB 2.0 test mode on the device port.

Usage: Write after the status stage of the SetFeature(TEST_MODE) request; leave the mode only by power cycle or reset.

Values:
0x0 test mode off (reset value);
0x1 Test_J;
0x2 Test_K;
0x3 Test_SE0_NAK;
0x4 Test_Packet;
0x5 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Port test mode. Starts a USB 2.0 test mode on the host port.

Usage: Write while the port is enabled; leave the mode by soft reset.

Values:
0x0 test mode off (reset value);
0x1 Test_J;
0x2 Test_K;
0x3 Test_SE0_NAK;
0x4 Test_Packet;
0x5 Test_Force_Enable (host only);
0x6 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Port speed. Shows the speed of the attached device.

Usage: Read after the enum interrupt.

Values:
0x0 high-speed;
0x1 full-speed (reset value);
0x2 low-speed;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Transmit region select. Chooses which transmit region fl_tx clears.

Usage: Write before fl_tx.

Values:
0x0 to 0xF device IN endpoint number (reset value 0x0);
0x10 host non-periodic region;
0x11 host periodic region;
0x12 to 0x1F reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

LPM answer. The handshake the device returns to an accepted LPM token.

Usage: Write before soft_conn; the fields have no effect when the build has no LPM.

Values:
0x0 ACK (reset value);
0x1 NYET;
0x2 STALL;
0x3 no response.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Transactions per microframe. For a high-bandwidth isochronous endpoint, the number of transactions in one microframe minus one.

Usage: Write before ep_en; 0 for other endpoint types.

Values:
0x0 one transaction (reset value);
0x1 two transactions;
0x2 three transactions;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Endpoint type. The USB transfer type of the endpoint.

Usage: Write before ep_en.

Values:
0x0 control (reset value);
0x1 isochronous;
0x2 bulk;
0x3 interrupt.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Transactions per microframe. For a high-bandwidth isochronous endpoint, the number of transactions in one microframe minus one.

Usage: Write before ep_en; 0 for other endpoint types.

Values:
0x0 one transaction (reset value);
0x1 two transactions;
0x2 three transactions;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Endpoint type. The USB transfer type of the endpoint.

Usage: Write before ep_en.

Values:
0x0 control (reset value);
0x1 isochronous;
0x2 bulk;
0x3 interrupt.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Transactions per microframe. For a periodic high-bandwidth channel, the count minus one.

Usage: Write before ch_en; 0 for other channels.

Values:
0x0 one transaction (reset value);
0x1 two transactions;
0x2 three transactions;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Device speed. The speed of the target device.

Usage: Write before ch_en; use full-speed or low-speed behind a hub with the split fields.

Values:
0x0 high-speed (reset value);
0x1 full-speed;
0x2 low-speed;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Endpoint type. The USB transfer type of the target endpoint.

Usage: Write before ch_en.

Values:
0x0 control (reset value);
0x1 isochronous;
0x2 bulk;
0x3 interrupt.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Transaction position. The position of the payload in a split isochronous OUT transaction.

Usage: Write before ch_en for split isochronous OUT.

Values:
0x0 middle (reset value);
0x1 end;
0x2 begin;
0x3 all.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Data PID. The data PID of the next packet; hardware toggles it.

Usage: Write DATA0 for a new transfer or after SETUP.

Values:
0x0 DATA0 (reset value);
0x1 DATA1;
0x2 DATA2;
0x3 MDATA.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.
